%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6626c84bb700413428bce8fec5aff79d, type: 3}
  m_Name: BeSubtle
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _description: 'the player talks to jessi as if she''s some sort of scared child,
    asking if there''s anything that happened to her that she might want to talk
    about.


    jessi refuses, saying that the player''s just gonna think of her
    less if she says anything. the player promises that there''s nothing jessi could
    say that would make her think lesser of her. while sounding like a sweet sentiment,
    it''s simply because the player''s opinion of jessi is already as low as it can
    go.


    jessi pauses. her gaze is off somewhere else, and the player waits
    patiently for her response. any second now, she can expect to get her answer.


    and
    she''s correct. jessi talks about how she didn''t get a chance at socialization
    because of the way she grew up: isolated from the rest of the world.


    she
    was the second child, up until the first one had gone missing. becoming the Only
    Child, her parents decided that they couldn''t possibly stand to lose another.
    they withdrew her from school and locked her in an empty room, safe from all
    harm''s way.


    but it was sooooo boring. sooooooo so so so so so so boring.
    all jessi could do was stare at the ceiling and hope that the next time she fell
    asleep, she''d awake to the sweet mercy of death. having such an empty life made
    death feel that much more fulfilling.


    she lived this way up until her late
    teenage years. as her parents got older, they weren''t as meticulous with their
    "care" of her anymore. and one day, as they left for errands, they forgot something
    so miniscule yet so important. they forgot to lock her door.


    jessi took
    no time to spring it open. having seen the rest of her house for the first time,
    it felt like she had just entered as an intruder. and so that she decided to
    be. she searched everywhere for any semblance of money, food, or water she could
    bring to get out of this retched place.


    and then with her legs that hardly
    walked a mile in their life, she ran. and here she landed. and here she would
    finally get to be a part of society, finally get to breathe the same air as everyone
    else, finally get to be a person.


    so why is it so hard? it''s so so so
    hard to get people to like her. why? why does it have to be this way? can''t
    everyone just welcome her back into the world? what''s wrong with everybody?


    after
    hearing this sob story, the player thinks to herself that it all makes terrible
    sense, and it''s kind of hilarious how much of it is so on-the-nose. jessi was
    literally forced into being a social recluse, and now she can''t break out of
    her fate. what a joke.


    but with the player''s approach, she knows that
    feigned sympathy is the best card she can play right now, so she attempts to
    comfort jessi. the world IS fucked up, isn''t it? but there''s sadly nothing
    else you can do. all we can do is live the life we''re meant to lead, whether
    we like it or not.


    jessi continues to look dazed, but she nods her head
    oh so slightly. there''s a sliver of a smile on her face. perfect, the player
    thinks. her satisfaction will do well for her proposition.'
  _sameOptionTarget: 0
  _lines:
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Jessi...
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Is there something that you've been grappling with that you haven't
      told me?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Huh?
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Well, I say this as an observer, but I believe that there's something
      deeper that's been troubling you.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: If that turns out to be true, I'd rather you tell me so we can
      clear the air.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: ...you'll just make fun of me.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: You'll say I'm pathetic and stupid or whatever and then I'll regret
      ever telling you.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Jessi.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I promise you that there's nothing you can say now that will make
      me think any lesser of you.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: In fact, whatever you tell me will further inform my opinion of
      you. Isn't that a good thing?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: ...
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I want to learn more about you, Jessi.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Tell me everything.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: ...
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: ...Sigh, fine.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: If you want to know that bad, I'll tell you.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: 'I had a brother, right? Keyword: had.'
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I guess he was just wandering around like an idiot and got himself
      kidnapped one day. At least that's what I heard.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I remember that day when I became an only child, my parents were
      freaking the fuck out over losing one of their kids.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: They kept trying to come up with shit to make sure I'd stay safe
      and that they wouldn't lose me.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Wanna know what their brightest idea was?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: To keep me locked up in my room forever.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: The emptiest room in the world.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: No windows because the glass could break and hurt me;
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: no blankets because I could suffocate myself while they weren't
      looking;
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: no decor on the walls because it could fall off and kill me.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: 'And the most important thing: no outside contact.'
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I was basically the safest kid to ever exist. I would basically
      just live forever without having to ever deal with the dangers of whatever
      the world could do to me.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: But it was so. Fucking. Boring.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: So mindnumbingly boring. So so so so so so so boring. So boring
      that I would go to bed hoping I wouldn't wake up. That the ceiling I stared
      at endlessly would just fall and crush me under its weight.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I looked forward to death more than I ever looked forward to life.
      If you can even call what I went through "living."
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Shit was like that up until I turned like...17? 18? It's hard
      to keep track of the days when every day is just the same.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I guess my parents were starting to lose their grip with age.
      I could taste it in the stale meals they gave me; somehow they got even staler
      with time.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: They were losing their edge and getting worse at making my daily
      life completely miserable.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: But that came with the best day of my life. The day they forgot
      to lock my door.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I couldn't even believe it at first, if I'm being real with you.
      It felt like I was having a dream for the first time in my life.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I flung my door open and the rest of the house just flashbanged
      me. I hadn't seen anything outside my room since I was, what, 5??
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: It was absolutely quiet. My parents weren't home that day.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Honestly felt like I was an intruder robbing my own house.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: So I guess I decided to play into that a bit.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I basically searched every edge of the house for as much money,
      food, and water that I could bring with me to get out of that damn place.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I came out with a lot more than I was expecting; damn hoarders
      keeping way too much fucking stuff.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: After I got what I thought was enough, I just got the fuck out
      of there as fast as I could.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: It felt weird to have the wind blow in my face for the first time
      in years, but it wasn't something that I hated.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: My legs hurt so bad trying to run because I had barely ever done
      that in my whole life, but I just sucked it up and kept running anyway.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: No way in HELL was I gonna lag behind and return to that miserable
      room. That dumb, lifeless, dull room that made me wish for death every day.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Then I just landed here. Far away enough from my home to feel
      alive.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I nearly pissed myself thinking about how excited I was to finally
      be a part of the world. How happy I was to finally just...exist like a normal
      fucking person, you know?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: But turns out the outside world is also full of shit.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Why the hell is it so hard to get along with people? They see
      you try and then they just tell you to fuck off and die?
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: It's so, so, so unfair. I just want to be welcomed back in the
      world and everyone decides they don't want to take me in.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: What the fuck is wrong with everybody? Why are they doing this
      to me??
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Why why why why why WHY???
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I hate it. I hate it all. I hate my stupid fucking brother, my
      stupid fucking parents, and the stupid FUCKING...EVERYBODY!!!
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: ...hah, that's quite the sob story if I've ever heard one.
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I'm impressed by how much it makes terrible, terrible sense.
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Frankly, it's comical how on-the-nose it is. Being forced into
      isolation and unable to break out of her socially impaired nature...it doesn't
      get any better than that.
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: I suppose sympathy is in order if I want to get her on my side.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: ...I'm sorry you had to endure all that, Jessi.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: The world truly is an unforgiving place, isn't it?
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: The lives we want to lead are often not the lives we're supposed
      to.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Sadly, there's nothing to be done about that. You can't change
      the system.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: You can only learn how to live alongside it and follow its logic,
      whether you like it or not.
  - _speaker: 0
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: An unfortunate truth, but nonetheless, the truth.
  - _speaker: 1
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: ...
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Her gaze continues to escape me. My concern quickly rises and
      dies in the same breath as she nods her head ever-so-slightly.
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: The corners of her mouth quirk upwards to form a sliver of a smile.
      Perfect.
  - _speaker: 2
    _charSprite: {fileID: 0}
    _CG: {fileID: 0}
    _music: {fileID: 0}
    _shakeCamera: 0
    _triggerHeartbeat: 0
    _maxFriendship: 0
    _dialogueLine: Such satisfaction will do well for the proposition I'm about to
      suggest.
  _playerReplyOptions: []
  _npcReplies: []
  _gameEnd: 1
